{"stage": "backlog", "event": "note", "category": "dispatch-deviation", "message": "Merged the sequence and validate steps into ONE agent call instead of two. Both read the same backlog and the validator must re-read the dependency graph anyway to check coverage, so splitting them pays two full context loads for one body of analysis. Budget-driven: F-1 consumed ~1.65M agent tokens end-to-end and 8.5 specs remain against ~14.8M, which leaves no margin at that rate. The combined agent is briefed to do BOTH jobs explicitly - cycle detection, topological waves, scope-disjointness verification file-by-file, AND coverage/well-formedness validation - so no check is dropped, only a context reload. Will apply to the remaining specs in the chain.", "at": "2026-10-15T00:27:42Z", "spec": "android-device-discovery-mirroring"}
